## Monorepo change workflow

Every `nornir-*` package (plus `dm4`) is a git submodule. An umbrella commit does not include
submodule file changes unless the pointer was updated, so the pointer bump is **part of the same
change**, not an optional follow-up:

1. Commit the code change inside the submodule.
2. Bump the umbrella pointer in a second commit, before pushing or rebuilding the dev container.
   Name the package and the issue: `Update nornir-buildmanager: recopy notes on content change, not mtime alone (#245)`

```bash
git submodule status          # no '+' lines when pointers match
git add nornir-<package>      # stage the pointer bump
git commit -m "Update nornir-<package>: <why>"
```

A `+` in `git submodule status` means the checkout differs from the recorded pointer (bump missing).
Without the bump, other clones and CI see the old submodule SHA, and a container recreate on a
bind-mounted checkout can look like work vanished (the entry script used to run
`git submodule update`, detaching each submodule at the recorded pointer even when local branches
were ahead). If you recreated before bumping, restore with `git -C nornir-<package> checkout dev`
(or your working branch): the commits are on the branch; only `HEAD` was detached.

Push order, remote-SHA checks and commit-only mode: [nornir-commit-push](../skills/nornir-commit-push/SKILL.md).

### Dev container submodule sync (bind-mounted workspace)

On container recreate, `cursor-dev-entry.sh` (mounted / default `cursor-dev` service):

- **Default:** `git submodule init` for missing submodules only; does not move existing checkouts.
  Warns when `git submodule status` shows `+`.
- **`NORNIR_SUBMODULE_UPDATE=1`:** full `git submodule update --init --recursive`, so checkouts match
  umbrella-recorded SHAs. Use after pointer bumps or to reset the tree to recorded commits on purpose.
- **`postAttachCommand`** (`NORNIR_CURSOR_DEV_SETUP_ONLY=1`) skips all git work; reattach alone does
  not reset submodules.
- **Clone mode** (`cursor-dev-clone`) always runs the full submodule update (appliance-style refresh).

## Scratch files

Never in the repository root: working notes, captured test output, debug dumps.

- Investigation notes and issue write-ups: `.cursor/issue-handoff/`.
- Test artifacts and debug images: `TESTOUTPUTPATH` (or `TEST_OUTPUT_DIR`), not the working tree.
- Logs: unified logging convention (`NORNIR_LOG_ROOT`); no ad hoc log files.
